From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:54:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Run Bluetooth at 3 Mbit/s

The Bluetooth link stayed at the controller's starting speed of
115,200 baud: the node set current-speed but no max-speed, so hci_bcm
never switched up. That is about 11 KB/s for all Bluetooth traffic.
A2DP audio crackled, and an HFP call link with mSBC carried no audio.

Set max-speed to 3 Mbit/s, the transport-speed of the ADT's
uart3/bluetooth node. The UART reaches it exactly from its 24 MHz
reference (oversampling 8, divisor 1).

On a J81 running Omarchy:
- The firmware patch loads in 0.83 s instead of 8.2 s.
- A2DP to a pair of headphones sounds much better; it crackled
  before.
- An HFP call link with the CVSD codec carries audio both ways: a tone
  reaches the headphones, and their microphone records. With mSBC it
  stays silent, as it did at 115,200 baud (CVSD was not tried there).

The SCO routing needs no setting: with and without
brcm,bt-pcm-int-params set to the transport, the microphone records
over CVSD, so the controller already routes SCO over HCI.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/195#issuecomment-7113896676
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index 64374d9da..9ee8b64f2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -224,7 +224,10 @@ &touchclk {
 /*
  * The BCM4350C2's Bluetooth on UART3, from the ADT uart3/bluetooth node:
  * power enable on D2207 GPIO 2, BT_WAKE on GPIO 164. m1n1 adds the device
- * address. 115,200 baud is the speed tested on a J81; the ADT allows 3 Mbit/s.
+ * address. The controller starts at 115,200 baud; the driver then switches
+ * the link to 3 Mbit/s, the ADT's transport-speed. At 115,200 baud, A2DP
+ * audio crackles, and an HFP call's SCO audio (64 kbit/s each way) does not
+ * fit.
  */
 &serial3 {
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart3_pins>;
@@ -235,6 +238,7 @@ &serial3 {
 	bluetooth: bluetooth {
 		compatible = "apple,j81-bcm4350c2-bt";
 		current-speed = <115200>;
+		max-speed = <3000000>;
 		shutdown-gpios = <&pmu_gpio 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		device-wakeup-gpios = <&pinctrl 164 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	};
